  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nIn [HTMLCanvasElement:toBlob(callback, type, quality)](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#dom-canvas-toblob) there is the sentence `Queue an element task on the canvas blob serialization task source given the canvas element to run these steps:` in step 4.2.\n\nIn the spec for (OffscreenCanvas:convertToBlob(options))[https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#dom-offscreencanvas-converttoblob] step 6.2 the exact sentence can be found.\n\nIt makes no sense there, as:\n- 1. The `OffscreenCanvas` is not a canvas element, and \n- 2. [Queue an element task](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#queue-an-element-task) can not be run without an element and in workers\n\nThere are two possible solutions:\n- Clarify, that the [placeholder canvas element](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#offscreencanvas-placeholder) is meant and that this task has to be run in the dom event queue? in some way?\n- Clarify what to do in cases, where this is run in the worker or inside the normal page, with global being a Window \n\n\nEither way, this needs more clarification on what exactly is meant in all cases, and not just a wrong copy paste from teh HTMLCanvasElement",
